From: prplMesh virtual-radio lab
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: tolerate unsupported reload when channel is unchanged

The NL80211 AP HAL persists the requested hostapd configuration and then uses
the non-standard `UPDATE` control command. Stock hostapd rejects that command.
During wireless-backhaul selection prplMesh reapplies the radio's existing
channel; treating the rejected no-op as fatal terminates the AP manager and
leaves AP autoconfiguration permanently incomplete.

Accept the operation when the requested channel and bandwidth already match
the live radio. Keep failing a genuine channel change so an unsupported
operation is never reported as successful.

--- a/common/beerocks/bwl/nl80211/ap_wlan_hal_nl80211.cpp
+++ b/common/beerocks/bwl/nl80211/ap_wlan_hal_nl80211.cpp
@@ -626,6 +626,13 @@ bool ap_wlan_hal_nl80211::set_channel(int chan, beerocks::eWiFiBandwidth bw, int
     // make hostapd reload its configuration file:
     const std::string cmd{"UPDATE "};
     if (!wpa_ctrl_send_msg(cmd)) {
+        if (m_radio_info.channel == chan &&
+            (bw == beerocks::eWiFiBandwidth::BANDWIDTH_UNKNOWN ||
+             m_radio_info.bandwidth == bw)) {
+            LOG(WARNING) << "Hostapd does not support '" << cmd
+                         << "'; live channel and bandwidth already match";
+            return true;
+        }
         LOG(ERROR) << "'" << cmd << "' command to hostapd failed";
         return false;
     }
